            "review_text": "Hardlyanexpert\nMelbourne, Australia149 contributions\n0\nSuch a disappointment this time.\nJun 2016 • Couples\nI have had takeaway from A Buu previously and was very impressed,so I was looking forward to a sit down meal there on my most recent trip to HCMC.After a false start trying to have lunch there (they open at 6pm) my wife and I went there around 9pm on a Monday evening.Upon entering,we were surprised to see that the place was completely empty apart from the staff.When we sat down to order our meals we were surprised for the second time when some sort of bug crawled out of my wife's menu when she opened it.Her scream was enough to wake the dead but it wasn't enough to get any of the staff to come over to see what had happened.With the bug eventually dealt with,we ordered a meal and drinks.I ordered what I was so impressed with last time,a chicken breast with mushroom sauce,and was eagerly awaiting it when we got surprise number three.The waitress came back to our table and told us that we couldn't have the chicken as the chef on duty that night didn't know how to cook it.Apparently their chef who knew how to grill a chicken breast and make mushroom sauce didn't turn up for work that evening so we were out of luck.I can't imagine that there would be too many restaurants that have an item on their menu that their chef can't actually cook,but this is Vietnam so nothing should surprise me.Maybe that's why the restaurant was empty when we walked in-the chef couldn't cook anything that anyone ordered.Anyway,after receiving that news,we simply got up and walked out and didn't bother trying again.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten June 22, 2016",
